  "description": "Pseudo-terminal backends behind one interface: ConPTY on Windows, forkpty on Linux and macOS. Spawns a child on a real pty, resizes it, and reports its exit. On Windows the package carries the open-source console host (conpty.dll + OpenConsole.exe — the one Windows Terminal and VS Code ship) and deploys it into your output directory, because the in-box conhost.exe crashes on some TUI teardowns and takes the shell with it.",
